15 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (PRISMA flowchart illustrating study selection: 3,496 records identified from five databases with 824 duplicates removed; 2,672 screened, 2,601 excluded; 71 reports sought plus 1 manually added; 72 assessed, 9 excluded; 63 studies included in review.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Two charts compare study modalities in a dataset of sixty-three studies: the left pie chart shows pathological at thirty-nine point seven percent, imaging at thirty-one point seven percent, molecular at nineteen percent, and clinical at nine point five percent; the right horizontal bar chart shows identical percentages and raw counts for each modality, confirming pathological studies are most frequent, followed by imaging, molecular, and clinical modalities.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Stacked area chart displays the number of studies in imaging, pathological, molecular, and clinical categories by publication year from 2019 to 2025, with a dashed line indicating total studies peaking in 2023 before declining.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Two horizontal error bar charts compare four data modalities \(clinical, molecular, pathological, imaging\) by AUC value \(left panel\) and accuracy \(right panel\). Each modality is represented by a colored dot with horizontal error bars, illustrating metric ranges. Clinical and imaging modalities show distinct spread and central values, with imaging having the widest range and lower central values compared to other modalities. Both panels have identical y-axis categories and legend indicating imaging modality.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Stacked area chart illustrating the number of studies published by year from 2019 to 2025 for four machine learning approach categories: Classic CNN, Lightweight CNN, Transformer/Hybrid, and Traditional ML. Classic CNN consistently shows the largest area, peaking in 2022 and 2023, while Transformer/Hybrid methods emerge in 2022 and grow until 2023. Traditional ML and Lightweight CNN also peak in 2023. Total studies per year are labeled near the peak of each area, with a decline across all categories after 2023.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Stacked bar chart with publication years from 2019 to 2025 on the x-axis and number of studies on the left y-axis compares green bars for single-modality studies and orange segments for multi-modality fusion. A blue dashed line with percentage markers shows increasing multi-modality percentages, starting at zero percent in 2019 and rising to thirty-three point three-three percent in 2025, indicating a trend toward more multi-modality studies over time.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
